findings.body:
The refactor in `get_config` changes `ApplePlatform.features` from `None` (when the feature list is empty) to `Some(ios_options.features)` unconditionally. This is an unrelated behavior change inside a PR that is described as a pure refactor. It is not mentioned in the changelog entry, and the commit message doesn't call it out.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-cli/src/mobile/ios/mod.rs" lines="268-279"}

Whether this matters depends on how `cargo_mobile2` treats `Some(vec![])` versus `None` when generating the Xcode project or build args. If it changes the generated project or passes an empty features argument, that would be a user-visible regression. Either restore the original conditional or split this change into its own commit with a justification.
